// expect: reject
// The check accepted `3 - 1.0` and the select then met an f64 where its
// scrutinee is typed i64 (soak nov25a, "no arm matches f64:2."). `s` is used
// in `g`, and its arithmetic is over `f`'s parameter: the cell that must be
// one numeric type reaches no variable of `g`'s scheme, but `g`'s close gave
// it to `g`'s instances, so `f`'s close never saw it and a call of `f` judged
// nothing. Such a cell waits for the definition around, which leaves it to
// its own instances: "type mismatch i64 does not contain f64".
{ let f = |a| { let g = |x| { let rec s = |n| select n { 0 => 0, _ => s(n - a) }; s(3) }; g(0) }; f(1.0) }
